 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Layers are your friend. A thin layer at the bottom, then the food, and another thin layer at the top. You can also use a small box of bread as both the base and the top. Keep the pack open so you can see the food and move it to the side as the sandwich gets closer. Dessert can wait. If it' small, you can wrap it in an empty calorie bar. For something warm, a sealed sushi roll works well. A few cubes of cheese are cheap and easy.",
